# Protocol Consistency — No Silent Confounds

A comparison is only valid if the cells differ in exactly the variable under study. Protocol drift between experiments has already produced one real confound; do not add another.

## Serialization / binning
ODDS data goes through `load_odds` with `binning="standard"` — values bucketed before serialization. The security loaders (`creditcard.py`, `unsw.py`) return **raw floats** — a documented protocol difference bounded by the M3.5 binned-creditcard arm.

**Any new loader or serialization path must state binned-vs-raw explicitly in its docstring and RunMetadata.** Any cross-experiment comparison of cells with different serialization must be flagged in the analysis — never presented as a pure domain effect.

*(Incident: Exp 3 raw-float vs Exp 2 binned — confounds the ODDS-vs-security narrative.)*

## Split protocol
AnoLLM protocol: **train = normals only; ALL anomalies go to test.** Splitting all rows 50/50 drops the train-half's anomalies from test — a silent bug with no error message.

Subsampled negatives are **always** importance-reweighted via `metrics.make_importance_weights`. Never report subsampled-prevalence AUPRC.

*(Incident: T3 — `prepare_creditcard` originally split all rows 50/50; caught on the real ULB download.)*

## Pinned dependencies — do not upgrade mid-study
`torch==2.3.1`, `pyod==2.0.1`, `transformers==4.48.2` are pinned in `uv.lock` for comparability. **Never bump these.** The pinned transformers does NOT support the Qwen3 architecture — that is why the models are Qwen2.5-3B / SmolLM, not Qwen3. A "helpful upgrade" breaks the AnoLLM fork stack and makes new cells incomparable to completed ones.

*(Incident: T1 — Qwen3 alias had to be reverted to Qwen2.5-3B for exactly this reason.)*

See also: `mode-a-scoring-constraint.mdc` for the related API-level constraint on Mode A log-prob availability.
